# Each of these stubs is the installed `solid-js@2.0.0-rc.3` the fixture's
# imports resolve through. Without the exception the stub is untracked, and in
# CI the fixture resolves no `solid-js` at all: dialect selection falls back to
# the default rather than reading a manifest, and the re-export and
# first-party-attribution claims below resolve against nothing. Coverage's
# `checkDialectStubs` fails on the untracked stub, which is what catches it.
# The nested consumer whose own top-level `import "solid-js"` is what the
# probe workspace's authenticated dependency closure has to resolve. Its stub
# is copied into the private workspace and *run* there, so an untracked one
# does not merely change the dialect in CI — it removes the only fixture that
# proves a consumer recipe can import the package under test at all.
# The dependency contract in this stub is the whole point of the fixture: it
# advertises host conditions, so it only resolves when the generator passes the
# analyzed target's export-map conditions through. Without this exception the
# stub is untracked and the fixture silently stops pinning that in CI.
# These three pin unknown-claim attribution. The stub selects the dialect and
# is otherwise unused by the exports under test (see the fixture READMEs), so
# without it the fixtures still generate, still pass, and pin nothing. They
# were repointed from 1.x to 2.0.0-rc.3 in the ADR 0110 retirement, and their
# expectations were regenerated against 2.0 with the claim intact.
# The partial dependency contract in this stub is the fixture: without it the
# consumer's import resolves to no contract at all and the obligation changes
# kind.
# ADR 0174: the same partial dependency contract, which opens every claim
# domain of the exports beside a proven owner requirement.
# ADR 0173: an rc.9-faithful effect/cleanup stub for the owner-call cover.
# Attribution-soundness fixtures. Each needs the solid-js stub for dialect
# selection; uncaptured-source-return additionally needs the partial
# `uncharted-helpers` contract, which is what makes its callee uncontracted.
# ADR 0146: the solid-js stub is what lets the generator see an accessor.
packages/wasm/browser.js
packages/wasm/generated.d.ts
packages/wasm/index.js
packages/wasm/solid-checker-wasm.wasi-browser.js
packages/wasm/solid-checker-wasm.wasi.cjs
packages/wasm/solid-checker-wasm.wasm32-wasi*.wasm
packages/wasm/wasi-worker*.mjs
packages/wasm/owned/
/.typefacts/

# Bulk phase-21 measurement dumps. These are 20-70 MB machine-readable
# artifacts of one measurement run each -- evidence a document cites, never an
# input any code or gate reads. 63 of them were tracked before this rule
# existed (961 MB, 21.3 M lines, 94% of the branch's whole diff), which is what
# the name-based list here failed to prevent: it enumerated some names and
# missed 42 others, and .gitignore never untracks what is already tracked.
#
# Structural now, not name-based, and the tracked copies were removed from the
# index on 2026-09-17. The files stay on disk; regenerate rather than commit.
# Documents citing one by relative link are citing a local artifact, not a
# repository file.

